WHY THIS AND NOT A curl. Every corpus path is behind the SITE_PASSWORD gate — GET
/commentaries/gen/1.json returns 307 to /gate — and the gate password is a credential this
session does not handle. Checking the LOCAL tree instead would prove only that the tree is
clean, not that the clean tree is what shipped, and 'measured the input, claimed the output'
is the exact shape this audit keeps finding.

METHOD. The deployment's own source archive, fetched from the Vercel API as the owning
account, decoded and extracted. This is the artifact Vercel serves from, so it answers the
delivery question directly and needs no site password:

  GET /v6/deployments/<id>/files                 -> src/.vercel/source.tgz.part1, .part2
  GET /v7/deployments/<id>/files/<uid>  x2       -> 139,810,147 + 98,974,975 bytes
  parts are {"data": "<base64>"} -> decode -> concatenate -> 179,088,823-byte tgz
  extract public/commentaries, scan with scripts/lib/served-corpus-authors.mjs

RESULT
  files scanned            1,212
  entries                  114,349
  offenders                NONE

  public/commentaries/gen/1.json, 126 entries, every author delivered:
    Adam Clarke | Alexander Maclaren | Augustine of Hippo | C.F. Keil & Franz Delitzsch
    Charles Haddon Spurgeon | Charles Hodge | Jamieson, Fausset & Brown | John Calvin
    John Gill | John Owen | John Wesley | Jonathan Edwards | Matthew Henry | Thomas Watson

  public/commentaries/_manifest.json — the index that made bulk collection a for-loop —
  advertises 28 sources / 114,349 entries and none of the quarantined authors.

